				{
					"Title": "Extreme rainfall",
					"Text1": "A 100-year rainfall occurs statistically once every hundred years. The highlighted areas on the model are the areas that are at risk of flooding via overland flooding during extreme rain. In houses with basements, water can also enter from the back via the pipe network. These flood risks are not visible in the model. When the municipality plans for new buildings, flood risks are taken into account and demands are made for various measures. It could, for example, be about raising the ground level and foundation level when building new houses. It is equally as important to ensure that large amounts of water have somewhere to go. One of the measures the municipality is working with is to create submerged surfaces in parks and natural areas. By making submerged surfaces in suitable places and creating them lower than surrounding buildings or roads, the water can collect there instead of causing flooding in places where it causes damage.",
					"Text2": "",
					"Datasource": "",
					"Legend1": "extremaregn",
